\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 Information ETE toolkit:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 \'a0\
The ETE (Eniviroment for Tree Exploration) toolkit can be used for making phylogenetic tree. The tool assist in analyzing and visualizing of making phylogenetic trees. We are using the ETE toolkit because it has extra functionalities with phylogenetic trees. This tool will help us generate from a newick-format to a well-structured phylogenetic tree.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
How to install the ETE toolkit:\
\'a0\
Go to your terminal and follow these steps:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf3 \'b7
\f2\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 python3 -m venv ete_env\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \

\f1 \'b7
\f2\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 source ete_env/bin/activate\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \

\f1 \'b7
\f2\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 pip install ete3\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 This allows us to install the ETE toolkit without admin privileges \uc0\u8232 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://etetoolkit.org/?utm"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul https://etetoolkit.org/}}\
\'a0\
